# Performance Test Plan & Results

## 1. Test Objectives
- Establish baseline performance metrics
- Identify bottlenecks under load
- Validate scalability requirements
- Detect performance regressions

## 2. Test Scenarios

### 2.1 Baseline Test
- **Users**: 100 concurrent
- **Duration**: 10 minutes
- **Goal**: Establish normal operation metrics
- **Success Criteria**: 
  - p95 < 500ms
  - Error rate < 0.1%
  - Throughput > 100 RPS

### 2.2 Load Test
- **Users**: 1,000 concurrent (ramp over 5 min)
- **Duration**: 30 minutes
- **Goal**: Validate expected production load
- **Success Criteria**:
  - p95 < 1000ms
  - Error rate < 0.5%
  - Throughput > 500 RPS

### 2.3 Stress Test
- **Users**: 3,000 concurrent (ramp over 10 min)
- **Duration**: 20 minutes
- **Goal**: Find breaking point
- **Success Criteria**:
  - Graceful degradation
  - No data corruption
  - Auto-scaling triggers

### 2.4 Spike Test
- **Users**: 500 → 5,000 → 500 (instant)
- **Duration**: 10 minutes
- **Goal**: Validate sudden traffic handling
- **Success Criteria**:
  - Recovery < 30 seconds
  - No cascading failures
  - Circuit breakers activate

### 2.5 Soak Test
- **Users**: 500 sustained
- **Duration**: 8 hours
- **Goal**: Detect memory leaks, resource exhaustion
- **Success Criteria**:
  - Memory stable
  - No connection leaks
  - Consistent response times

## 3. Key Metrics to Monitor

| Metric | Target | Alert Threshold |
|--------|--------|-----------------|
| Response Time (p50) | < 200ms | > 500ms |
| Response Time (p95) | < 1000ms | > 2000ms |
| Response Time (p99) | < 2000ms | > 5000ms |
| Error Rate | < 0.1% | > 1% |
| Throughput | > 500 RPS | < 100 RPS |
| CPU Utilization | < 70% | > 85% |
| Memory Utilization | < 75% | > 90% |
| Database Connections | < 80% pool | > 95% pool |

## 4. Sample Results (Load Test - 1000 Users)

### Response Times
| Endpoint | p50 | p95 | p99 | Max |
|----------|-----|-----|-----|-----|
| GET /products | 45ms | 180ms | 320ms | 890ms |
| POST /cart | 65ms | 220ms | 410ms | 1.2s |
| POST /checkout | 180ms | 650ms | 1.1s | 3.4s |
| GET /orders | 55ms | 200ms | 380ms | 950ms |

### System Resources
- **CPU**: Avg 45%, Peak 68%
- **Memory**: Avg 2.1GB, Peak 3.4GB
- **Database CPU**: Avg 35%, Peak 55%
- **Database Connections**: Avg 45, Peak 78
- **Network I/O**: Avg 12 MB/s, Peak 45 MB/s

### Errors Observed
- 0.02% timeout errors on checkout (3rd party payment)
- 0% application errors

## 5. Bottleneck Analysis

### Identified Bottlenecks
1. **Checkout Service**: Synchronous payment processing
   - *Impact*: p99 1.1s on checkout
   - *Recommendation*: Async payment with webhook confirmation

2. **Product Search**: Unindexed category filter
   - *Impact*: 320ms p99 on product listing
   - *Recommendation*: Add composite index on (category, price)

3. **Order History**: N+1 query problem
   - *Impact*: Linear degradation with order count
   - *Recommendation*: Eager loading / batch fetching

## 6. Optimization Recommendations

### Quick Wins (1-2 days)
- Enable response compression (gzip/brotli)
- Add database connection pooling tuning
- Implement query result caching for catalog

### Medium Term (1-2 weeks)
- Async payment processing
- Database index optimization
- CDN for static assets

### Long Term (1+ months)
- Microservice decomposition for checkout
- Event-driven architecture
- Edge computing for geo-distribution

## 7. Regression Detection
- Automated comparison with baseline (k6 thresholds)
- Alert on > 10% p95 degradation
- Alert on > 5% throughput decrease
- Weekly trend analysis dashboard
